titre$I. OLARIAGA & I. SALCEDO : CANTHARELLUS OCCURRING IN THE MEDITERRANEAN AREA
com$ /adapt GF nov 2013
rem$LANGUE$Anglais

1,2$ a) Pileus partially to entirely covered by a white or pink coating at least when young, even when exposed to the light; hymenophore white or bright orange
1,4$ b) Pileus without a white coating even when young, paler in unexposed parts; hymenophore never bright orange
1,10$ Source
2,0$ a) Hymenophore often orange-yellow when young, later remaining so near the margin; sporeprint orange-yellow; basidiospores 7-9,5-( 11) x (4)-4,5-5,2 mm $ C. pallens
2,3$ b) Hymenophore ochre white when young, not orange-yellow near the margin; sporeprint pale yellowish ochre; basidiospores 9-12,5 x 4-6 mm
3,0$ a) Pileus partially to entirely pink when young $ c. lilacinopruinatus
3,0$ b) Pileus without pink tones $ C. alborufescens
4,0$ a) Pileus citrine yellow to light yellow-orange in wet conditions; sometimes with olive or brownish tones; basidiomata usually not fleshy $ C. ferruginascens
4,0$ b) Pileus bright orange in wet conditions; without olive or brownish tones; basidiomata usually fleshy $ C. ilicis


10,0$ CANTHARELLUS ILICIS SP. NOV., A NEW SPECIES FROM THE MEDITERRANEAN BASIN COLLECTED IN EVERGREEN QUERCUS FORESTS/// Revista Catalana de Micologia, vo!. 30: 107-116; 2008.